# Rancher Manager

Rancher is installed and bootstrapped: ${rancher_url}

| | |
|---|---|
| Rancher version | `${rancher_version}` |
| cert-manager version | `${cert_manager_version}` |
| TLS source | `${tls_source}` |
| Replicas | ${replicas} |

## Admin access

The admin credentials (username `admin`, password, API token) are stored in
AWS Secrets Manager (region `${region}`), not in meshStack:

- Secret name: `${admin_secret_name}`
- Secret ARN: `${admin_secret_arn}`

Fetch them with
`AWS_REGION=${region} scripts/fetch-rancher-admin.sh ${admin_secret_name}`, or
`aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --region ${region} --secret-id ${admin_secret_name} --query SecretString --output text`.

%{ if tls_source == "rancher" ~}
The UI uses a certificate from a Rancher-generated CA. Browsers will warn until
you trust that CA or switch `tls_source` to `letsEncrypt` or `secret`.
%{ endif ~}
